    "credential_change_note": "Password change and KDF upgrade replace only descriptor/head in one CAS transaction. Existing record/index bytes and record revisions stay unchanged; latest retries write nothing but reauthenticate the supplied new credential through the current admitted KDF. Credential operation tags cover public operation metadata and the encrypted descriptor hash, never password guesses. Unadmitted/invalid/no-op/downgrade targets reject; unknown outcomes block use until exact new-header reconciliation. The explicit 65536KiB/4-pass upgrade is the smallest pass-count increase over the baseline experiment, not a new production default. Four numeric rejection inputs are negative fixture variants; one successful writer and zero content writes are required transaction invariants.",
