      "key_bits": 128,
      "maximum_frontier_nodes": 129,
      "delete_maximum_captured_nodes": 130,
      "derivation": "Two is the explicit caller page-size fixture. Five records produce two full pages and a partial final page; the canonical binary tree has nine nodes. Frontier129 and selected delete path129 plus one promoted sibling130 derive from the128-bit key format. None is a newly selected product page/population/latency quota.",
      "contract": "Opaque Engine cursor and pending proof stay in Rust; JS fetches one requested node/row inside one IndexedDB readonly snapshot per page. Each physical row is envelope-digest verified before publication. Complete requires traversal/count finality, while each prefix proves only its members. Changed descriptor/head, lock or any failed page cancels continuation; no historical-root pin or cross-transaction snapshot promise.",
      "mutation_contract": "Maintained save_at/prepare_save_at and delete_at/prepare_delete_at require caller original head digest plus record revision before draft preparation, followed by transaction CAS. Caller head is captured/copied before transport waits. Revision-only fixture methods/actions are explicitly diagnostic. Unknown outcomes remain unknown and reconcile by operation ID; exact current-head latest retry is zero-write.",
      "access_profile": "P2 only; strict130-byte descriptor admission remains. P3 recovery/provider and root-rotation browser bridges remain unsupported and are qualified only in their separately named native/synthetic experiments."
